def list_from_node(node,ctx):
    items=[]
    for li in node.children:
        if not isinstance(li,Node) or li.tag!="li": continue
        blocks=blocks_from_children(li.children,ctx)
        # Convert Para to Plain if item is a single para and original list was tight? HTML does not encode tightness except p tags: an li content with direct text -> blocks_from_children creates Para for inline text. In pandoc HTML reader, list items without <p> become Plain; our blocks_from_children can't distinguish. Check if li children contain a p node: if no block-level p, convert first/only Para to Plain.
